---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who runs Humans on Mars, what it is for, and how to report a correction.">
  <section class="prose-wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="display-sm">An independent guide to life on Mars</h1>
      <p>
        Humans on Mars helps curious adults, educators and students picture everyday life on another planet: the time, the
        gravity, the distance from home, and what it would take to stay alive. We combine interactive tools with explainers that
        cite their sources.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are independent. We are not affiliated with SpaceX, NASA, ESA or any other agency or company. When we describe a plan,
        we name who announced it and when, and we do not treat plans as achievements.
      </p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot an error, tell us and we will check it against the primary source, fix it, and note the change on the page.
        <!-- TODO: add a contact address once Kevin chooses one. -->
      </p>
      <h2>Images</h2>
      <p>Artwork of imagined settlements and daily life is labelled as concept art. Mission imagery carries its credit.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
